{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"13/10/2026 22:45:10","profile":{"player_id":"73612","last_updated":"13/10/2026 22:45","fullname":"Ismat Alam","short_display_name":"I Alam","name":"Ismat Alam","gender":"M","dob":"02/02/2002","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Afghanistan","nationality_id":"262","nationality":"Afghanistan","nationality_short_code":"AFG","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"3","text":"All Rounder","role":"All Rounder"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"10","text":"Right-arm fast medium"},"writeup":"<p>Born on February 2, 2002, in Nangarhar, Afghanistan, Ismat Alam is a dynamic right-handed all-rounder who bowls right-arm fast-medium. Coming from a notable cricketing family (as the nephew of international fast bowler Aftab Alam), Ismat has rapidly ascended through Afghanistan's domestic structure to make an impression on the international stage.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Alam made his first-class debut in November 2022, steadily honing his red-ball credentials in regional multi-day competitions. His domestic breakthrough arrived during the 2024-25 Ahmad Shah Abdali 4-day Tournament, where he played a starring role for the Pamir Legends. Finishing as the tournament's leading run-scorer, he amassed 723 runs from six matches at an astonishing average of 103.23, highlighted by a magnificent, career-best knock of 263 not out.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>His stellar domestic form earned him a Test cap for Afghanistan, making his debut against Zimbabwe on January 2, 2025, at Bulawayo. Making a historic entrance into Test cricket batting from the lower order (No. 8 or below), he struck a brilliant century (101).&nbsp;In white-ball formats, Alam has represented regional powerhouses like the Speen Ghar Region (Speenghar Tigers) in the Shpageeza Cricket League, showcasing his multi-dimensional utility with aggressive lower-middle-order hitting and sharp fast-medium spells.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Expanding his international exposure, he also featured for Afghanistan in white-ball setups, including the Asian Games Men&rsquo;s T20I tournament in September 2026 and was also picked in the Afghan squad for the one-off Test against Bangladesh in Abu Dhabi, in October 2026.</p>","relation":[{"id":10101,"name":"Aftab Alam","relation":"Uncle","relation_id":13}],"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1188","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Afghanistan"},{"id":"1550","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Afghanistan A"},{"id":"1603","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Speen Ghar Region"},{"id":"1609","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Band-e-Amir Dragons"},{"id":"1613","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Speen Ghar Tigers"},{"id":"1875","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Biratnagar Kings"},{"id":"3091","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Pamir Legends"},{"id":"3092","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Hindukush Strikers"},{"id":"3966","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Maiwand Champions"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"1","comp_type":"Test International - m","match_id":"253605","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/253605/zimbabwe-vs-afghanistan","series_id":"8304","series_name":"Afghanistan in Zimbabwe, 2 Test Series, 2024/25","match_date":"02/01/2025","for":{"id":"1188","text":"Afghanistan","short_name":"AFG"},"vs":{"id":"10","text":"Zimbabwe","short_name":"ZIM"},"venue":{"id":"129","text":"Queens Sports Club, Bulawayo"},"batting":{"runs":"101","balls_faced":"183","hundreds":"1","innings":[{"number":"1","runs":"","balls_faced":"2","hundreds":""},{"number":"2","runs":"101","balls_faced":"181","hundreds":"1"}]},"bowling":{"wickets":"","runs_given":"7","ball_bowled":"18","economy":"2.33","five_wk_haul